    {
      "id": "be-s10-procuring-inputs-c1",
      "heading": "The manager's role",
      "explanation_md": "A manager has two jobs here:\n\n- **Procure inputs in the least cost manner**, which puts the firm on its cost curve at a point like **B**.\n- **Provide incentives** for workers to put forth effort.\n\nFail at these and the firm ends up at a point like **A**: at 10 units of output it spends **$100** instead of **$80**. To reach B, managers must **use all inputs efficiently** and **acquire inputs by the least costly method**.",
      "example_ids": [
        "be-ex-points-a-and-b"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Point B is on the cost curve (least cost); point A is above it because inputs were bought or used badly.",
      "clarification": null,
