    {
      "id": "be-s10-procuring-inputs-c2",
      "heading": "Three ways to get inputs",
      "explanation_md": "| Method | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| **Spot exchange** | Buyer and seller meet, exchange, and then go their separate ways |\n| **Contract** | A legal document that creates an extended relationship between a buyer and a seller |\n| **Vertical integration** | The firm shuns other suppliers and produces the input internally |",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [
        {
          "term": "Spot exchange",
          "meaning": "Buyer and seller of an input meet, exchange, and then go their separate ways",
          "source_ref": "be--session-10#4"
        },
        {
          "term": "Vertical integration",
          "meaning": "A firm shuns other suppliers and produces an input internally",
          "source_ref": "be--session-10#4"
        }
      ],
      "exam_line": "Spot exchange: one-off. Contract: extended legal relationship. Vertical integration: make it yourself.",
      "clarification": null,
